hologists  and is  approved by CLIA for the performance of high complexity testing       Fluorescence in situ Hybridization  FISH  Report  HER 2 neu    Result  AMPLIFIED  The Her 2 cen 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE    Specimen Site Type  Left Breast Core Tissue    Indication for Study  Evaluate for Her 2 neu Gene Amplification    The average of Her 2 neu copies per tile  REMOVED_DATE    The average of cen17 copies per tile  REMOVED_DATE    The cutoff point for assessing Her 2 neu gene amplification is a  Her 2 cen17 ratio greater than REMOVED_DATE    The specimen is considered AMPLIFIED for the Her 2 neu gene     A total of 179 tiles from this patient s tissue were analyzed by the Vysis  AutoVysion System and were sufficient for analysis     This patient specimen resulted in a Her 2 cen17 value of REMOVED_DATE and is  therefore considered amplified for the HER 2 gene  The  average HER 2 copy number was REMOVED_DATE copies per tile  Although the  biological and clinical basis for gene amplification is not  clear  it has been observed that the most aggressive disease stage is  associated with the highest frequency of gene  amplification  The HER 2 status of a tumor is a critical determinant of  response to trastuzumab based treatment  Benefit  correlates best with tumors that are determined to be amplified by  fluorescence in situ hybridization for HER 2  Clinical  correlation is advised     FISH was performed using the PathVysionHER 2 DNA Probe Kit     Probe Name Detection Parameters Result ISCN    PathVysion amplification of the HER 2 gene AMPLIFIED nuc  ish  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID x3  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID x14     Electronically Signed by Galina Bannykh  M D on REMOVED_DATE at US LABS    Methodology and Intended Use  Please see US Labs report     Disclaimer  This Test was performed at  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Campus Drive  Irvine  CA   REMOVED_CASE_ID     The PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit has been approved by the U S  Food    Drug Administration  FDA  for detecting amplification 