Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  ELIZABETH A RAFFERTY  M D  Resident  Elizabeth Demicco  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Melinda J Lerwill  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Right breast area of architectural distortion    malignancy  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  SOLID PAPILLARY DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  FOCAL MICROINVASION CANNOT BE EXCLUDED  NOTE  The tumor cells are positive for synaptophysin and focally positive for chromogranin  consistent with neuroendocrine differentiation  Immunostains for p63  calponin  SM MHC  and cytokeratin support that the majority of the tumor sampled represents in situ carcinoma  but the focus concerning for microinvasion is no longer present on the deeper immunostained sections  Receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  are six cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note 