nal of Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID             Electronically Signed Out By  Elena F  Brachtel MD on REMOVED_DATE 16 09       CLINICAL HISTORY  56 year old female with left axillary lymph node excision demonstrating  metastatic adenocarcinoma  consistent with breast origin  Post excision breast  MRI demonstrated multiple areas of prompt non mass like enhancement in the upper  outer left breast  One of these areas was biopsied via MRI guidance    IDC vs   other     SPECIMENS SUBMITTED   A  BREAST CORE BIOPSY  LEFT    GROSS DESCRIPTION  A  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  x 0 2cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue admixed with presumed blood coagulant   submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID          PART   BREAST CORE BIOPSY  LEFT       report_end  , Core biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 41 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast 50 year old female with right breast cancer 7 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 11 18                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 2 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A  Gross Description by  JIM BRADLEY Resident  SONER ALTIOK  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Eren D Yeh  M D  Stephanie Eisenstat MD PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Core biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CONNIE ROCHE  NP KENNY C LAI  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 56 year old woman with very dense breast with indeterminate focus of enhancement seen in the medial left breast on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS   MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy reveal a rare cluster of angulated ducts infiltrating the stroma which are present over an area measuring approximately 0 2cm  Adjacent to the lesion is a 0 3cm cluster of ducts which are expanded by a proliferation of monomorphic ductal cells arranged in a micropapillary pattern lining the duct structures  The morphologic findings are compatible with a diagnosis of invasive tubular carcinoma arising in association with low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ  To help confirm these diagnoses  we performed level sections and a panel of immunostains on the core biopsy  Multiple level sections show the DCIS to better advantage  An immunostain for keratin REMOVED_DATE shows focal loss of staining in luminal cells and supports the diagnosis of DCIS  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrate absence of the myoepithelial layer in the infiltrating ducts and supports the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  Overall  the findings are limited due to limited sampling of the lesion  however  based on morphology and immunohistochemistry  the findings are compatible with well differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma and low grade ductal carcinoma in situ  Dr  David Wilbur has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  aggregate of multiple tan yellow to gray white fibroadipose tissue cores  which are submitted in toto  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday August 31   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 51 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left    Core biopsy  report_end  , Core biopsy.
