ted as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name   unit number and  right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm oriented mastectomy specimen with a long stitch at 12 o clock position and a short stitch at the axilla  The overlying tan brown skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm and contains REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm areola with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm nipple  which are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  anterior blue  posterior black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white  firm to hard  irregular  C shaped mass in the outer mid and the lower quadrant  which lies 0 6cm from posterior inked margin and 1 5cm from the anterior inked margin  The breast tissue adjacent to this mass is tan white and fibrous  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows diffuse tan white fibrous tissue  The fat in the upper outer quadrant shows diffuse fat necrosis  Three possible lymph nodes are dissected ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  tan white mass in the outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tan white fibrous tissue adjacent to the mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections  upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section  lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Three possible lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fibrous tissue medial to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative fibrous tissue lateral to mass  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_