dendum  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast ultrasound core   are five cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  left breast area core anterior   are multiple cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm which are submitted in toto as cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Also received in the same container is a blue cassette which is opened to reveal three fibrofatty tissue cores measuring from REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm to REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm which are submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  A large component of the tumor does not stain for progesterone receptor protein  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal imm