rmined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 22 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow fibrofatty lumpectomy specimen inked and sectioned to reveal diffuse fibroelastic white tissue  There are two firm nodules of white gray granular gritty tissue abutting the inked margin  Each of these nodules are a few millimeters apart measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x0 7cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm respectively  One section containing both nodules is frozen as FX 1  now in A  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in B F  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm of thin membraned  yellow gelatinous foreign body consistent with a silicone implant  The specimen is for gross only  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  silicone implant left  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm gelatinous thin membraned  foreign body consistent with a silicon implant  The specimen is for gross diagnosis only  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional right breast tissue  is a large fragment of tan yellow focally white fibrofatty piece of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  Also received in the same jar is a smaller tan white fibrofatty fragment measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  In addition  in the same jar there is a tan white smooth  piece of fibrous soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm  The larger fragment is serially sectioned to reveal tan white firm fibrous parenchyma with focal areas of yellow lobated fat  The specimen is submitted in entirety in G K  The smaller fragment is bivalved to reveal a tan white fibrous cut surface  This small fragment as well as the serially sectioned  thin membranous piece are submitted entirely in L M  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INVASIVE CARCINOMA IS PRESENT AT THE INKED MARGIN  O R  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Robert Henry Young  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  James Warren May Jr   M D  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  IMPLANT  RIGHT BREAST  PART C  IMPLANT  LEFT BREAST  PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL MARGIN , No breast biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 59 CLINICAL DATA  Breast and nipple biopsy    Paget s disease                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   EXTENDING TO THE INKED MARGIN IN SEVERAL AREAS  AND FOCALLY INTO THE DERMIS OF THE OVERLYING SKIN  LYMPHATIC INVASION IS IDENTIFIED  2  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  5   NOTE  Paget s disease is not seen  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 54                                                                                     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   13  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 5  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 57     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 31     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue and overlying skin with schirrous retraction  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm white infiltrating lesion abutting the skin surface  Representative sections frozen as frozen section  1 which is kept frozen  BRDU sent  Frozen section sent for ER and PR analysis  Remainder is submitted in cassettes A through D  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Incisional biopsy.
