ATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR  RECEPTOR PROTEINS    Breast  Right  12 00  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein   The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2   See note     Note   Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive  nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows     The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained     Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained     Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained     The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained     HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is  evaluated visually and reported as follows     Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or  incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells     Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane  immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells     Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in    30  of tumor cells     These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by  the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not  been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The  FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this  laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision       Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 15    REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 11 35PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses       ADDENDUM NOTE  Using immunoperoxidase methods  the invasive tumor cells  express e cadherin  consistent with a carcinoma of ductal type             Addendum  2 by John H Eichhorn M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH  15   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 32 29PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses                 ADDENDUM NOTE   REASON   2 RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH   FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION    Breast  Right  12 00  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified    See note     Note  The average ratio of HER 2 signals to chromosome 17 signals varies from  1 5 to REMOVED_DATE depending on the area of tumor selected for FISH analysis  The  ratio is affected by the presence of only one chromosome 17 signal rather than  two signals in many tumor cells  This may reflect failure to detect two  chromosomes in many tumor cells rather than absence of second chromosome 17   As the tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 by immunohistochemistry   it is likely that there is no HER 2 gene amplification in the tumor cells in  this biopsy  However  FISH analysis should be repeated when the tumor is  excised   Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 signals  398  to chromosome  17 signals  237  in 180 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or  equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17  polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis   The results at or near the cutoff point  ranging from REMOVED_DATE   2 2  should be  interpreted with caution  Equivocal Amplification   Reference  Journal of  Clinical Oncology 25 118 145   REMOVED_CASE_ID          Addendum  3 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 21    REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 02 52 06PM  By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final  Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed  or corrected the diagnoses     PART   Breast  Right  12 00   Core biopsy       report_end  , Core biopsy.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 10 08 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 18 27                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm aggregate of soft  tan cores of tissue  which are submitted in toto in Cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Alphonse Taghian  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY , Core biopsy.
